[statement]
A removal that follows the replacement of the package that needed it
waits until the walk has placed what placing the replacement led to:
`a` 2, which no longer needs `six`, triggers `apyc` 2, whose condition
names it, and `apyc` needs `d`. apk upgrades `a`, installs `d`, upgrades
`apyc`, and only then removes `six`. The rule of
`reduced/picard-removes-py3-six-after-py3-dateutil-pyc`.

[repository]
P:a
V:2

P:apyc
V:2
i:a=2
D:d

P:d
V:1

P:app
V:2
D:a=2

[installed]
P:apyc
V:1

P:six
V:1

P:a
V:1
D:six

P:app
V:1
D:a

[world]
app

[request]
app>1

[answer apk-tools 3.0.9-r0]
upgrade a 1 2
install d 1
upgrade apyc 1 2
remove six 1
upgrade app 1 2
